I   WARN profile-ops: --profile-ops times every op, which restores synchronisations
I        why: the run is slower and its numbers are not comparable against an unprofiled one
I        fix: drop --profile-ops for anything measured
I   note experts-from-host: 12.49 GiB of weights a rank live in the pinned host pool and cross PCIe when they are used
I        why: a prefill step streams every routed layer's pooled experts onto the card, so its speed is bounded by the link; decode reads the ones it routes to
I        fix: more VRAM for the experts: a shorter --max-model-len or fewer --max-num-seqs, --embedding-placement ram, --kv-cache-dtype fp8, or more cards (--tp)
